  "id": "COMPOUND:160 - PROTEIN:702",
  "verbalization": "Menadione, a form of vitamin E, is implicated in the relationship with Multidrug resistance-associated protein 1 (MRP1) through a chain of targets that involves Coagulation factor V and Procaine benzylpenicillin. The evidence suggests that menadione may act as a target for these molecules, which in turn target MRP1. This pathway is consistent across three distinct paths, each linking menadione to MRP1 via different intermediaries. The high scores in all three paths indicate a strong, reliable connection, though the exact mechanism by which menadione influences these intermediaries remains unclear. The presence of multiple independent pathways reinforces the likelihood of a functional link, though the precise role of menadione in this process requires further investigation.",
